# Autoreel configuration.
#
# Nothing here is required. The app runs with an empty environment — every AI
# capability falls back to an offline stand-in, and social publishing simply
# stays unavailable until you configure a platform.
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in what you need.

# --- Where things are stored ------------------------------------------------

# Videos, settings and the job queue. Defaults to ~/.autoreel
# Rendering writes a lot of intermediate frames and audio, so point this at a
# disk with room if your home directory is small.
# AUTOREEL_DATA_DIR=/var/lib/autoreel

# --- AI providers -----------------------------------------------------------
#
# These can also be set in the app under Settings, which is usually easier —
# keys entered there are stored in the data directory and take effect without
# a restart. A key set here is used only when the stored one is absent.

# Claude writes the scripts. Without it, scripts come from a template.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# Overrides the script model. Defaults to a current Sonnet model.
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5

# Voiceover and visuals. Without it, narration is silent (timed to the words)
# and visuals are gradients in your chosen art style.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# OPENAI_TTS_MODEL=tts-1-hd
# OPENAI_IMAGE_MODEL=gpt-image-1

# --- Publishing -------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Each platform needs an app you register with that platform, and each reviews
# apps before it will accept a post. There is no shortcut around this and no
# credential this project could ship to avoid it.
#
# Restart after setting these — the Connect buttons in Settings only appear for
# platforms whose credentials are present.

# Where this app is reachable. Used to build OAuth redirect URIs, which must
# match what you registered with each platform exactly.
# Required for Instagram at all (see below).
# PUBLIC_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# TikTok — developers.tiktok.com, "Content Posting API".
# Note: until your app passes TikTok's audit, posts land as private drafts.
# TIKTOK_CLIENT_KEY=
# TIKTOK_CLIENT_SECRET=

# YouTube — Google Cloud console, YouTube Data API v3 enabled.
# Note: an unverified OAuth client can only upload as `private`.
# YOUTUBE_CLIENT_ID=
# YOUTUBE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Instagram — Meta app with instagram_content_publish, and a business or
# creator account linked to a Facebook Page.
#
# Instagram does not accept an uploaded file: it fetches the video over HTTP
# from a URL you give it. So PUBLIC_BASE_URL must be an address reachable from
# the public internet — a tunnel or a small server. On a laptop with no such
# address, Instagram publishing cannot work. TikTok and YouTube take the bytes
# directly and have no such requirement.
# INSTAGRAM_CLIENT_ID=
# INSTAGRAM_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- Rendering --------------------------------------------------------------

# ffmpeg and ffprobe ship as npm packages and are found automatically. Set
# these only to use your own build.
# FFMPEG_PATH=/usr/bin/ffmpeg
# FFPROBE_PATH=/usr/bin/ffprobe
